-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Jack the Nipper
  Publisher   Gremlin Graphics, 1986
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Jack the Nipper (1986)(Gremlin Graphics Software)[a].z80
  MD5         4c5398b8bcfd88ebd83656f01c3aca21

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Every figure painted in colours of its own instead of the room's
              ink: Jack, the grown-ups, the pickups and the effects. Only
              sprite colours change. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Changes     1.0: figures as Next sprites; Enhanced colours (every figure
              painted) as a menu choice.

  Note        Jack, the grown-ups, the pickups and the effects (the pea,
              sparkles, smoke) are hardware sprites, so a figure no longer
              takes the colours of the room it crosses; the rooms, the panel
              and the text stay as the game draws them. It runs about 2%
              slower than the original.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Immunity
   2  Infinite lives

  Immunity is the archive's POKE (the lose-a-life call skipped); Infinite
  lives jumps over the lives count and its redraw. Both checked against the
  code.

